@startuml

title RoomClimateNode - Regular Measurement Cycle

hide footbox
autonumber
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam ParticipantPadding 18

actor "ESP32\nstartup" as Startup
participant "RoomClimate\nController" as Controller
participant "WiFiConnection\nManager" as WiFi
participant "MqttClient\nService" as MQTT
participant "Sht31Driver" as SHT31
participant "ESP32Battery\nDriver" as Battery
participant "Sensor\nCoordinator" as Coordinator
participant "MqttMeasurement\nPublisher" as Publisher
participant "PowerManager" as Power

note over Startup, Controller
  Each timer wake-up starts a new application boot.
  This diagram shows the regular cycle without an OTA request.
end note

== Initialization ==
Startup -> Controller: init()
activate Controller
Controller -> WiFi: init()
Controller -> MQTT: init()
Controller -> SHT31: init()
Controller -> Battery: init()
Controller --> Startup: return
deactivate Controller

== Connection ==
Startup -> Controller: update()
activate Controller
Controller -> WiFi: connect()
Controller -> WiFi: isConnected()
WiFi --> Controller: connection status

break Wi-Fi connection failed
  Controller -> Power: enterDeepSleep()
  note right of Power
    Deep sleep is entered only if
    timer wake-up configuration succeeds.
  end note
end

Controller -> MQTT: connect()
Controller -> MQTT: isConnected()
MQTT --> Controller: connection status

break MQTT connection failed
  Controller -> Power: enterDeepSleep()
end

== OTA status and request check ==
ref over Controller, MQTT: Publish "window_closed" and firmware version;\nsubscribe and poll for OTA requests (up to 2 s)
note over Controller
  Calls MqttOtaStatusPublisher, MqttFirmwareVersionPublisher,
  and MqttOtaRequestReader. OTA maintenance is omitted here
  and will be covered in a separate OTA sequence diagram.
end note

== Measurement acquisition ==
Controller -> SHT31: readMeasurements()
Controller -> Battery: readVoltage()
Controller -> Coordinator: readAllSensors()
activate Coordinator
note right of Coordinator
  Retrieves cached values via TemperatureSensor,
  HumiditySensor, and BatterySensor.
  Does not trigger another hardware measurement.
end note
Coordinator --> Controller: Measurements
deactivate Coordinator

note over Controller
  SensorValidator.validateAllSensors(measurements)
  StateMachine.calculateState(validationResults)
  Both results are currently ignored by the publishing logic.
end note

== MQTT publishing ==
Controller -> Publisher: publish(measurements)
activate Publisher
Publisher -> MQTT: publish(temperature, retain=true)
MQTT --> Publisher: bool
Publisher -> MQTT: publish(humidity, retain=true)
MQTT --> Publisher: bool
Publisher -> MQTT: publish(battery level, retain=true)
MQTT --> Publisher: bool
Publisher --> Controller: true if all succeeded
deactivate Publisher

== Deep sleep ==
Controller -> MQTT: disconnect()
Controller -> Power: enterDeepSleep()
note right of Power
  Configures a 15-minute timer wake-up,
  then starts deep sleep if configuration succeeds.
end note

deactivate Controller

@enduml
